sketchBlocks.bodyMarkdown:
As persistence grows, route handlers become easier to read when SQL lives in focused data-access functions.

```js
function listEvents(category) {
  if (category) {
    return db
      .prepare("SELECT id, title, category FROM events WHERE category = ?")
      .all(category);
  }

  return db
    .prepare("SELECT id, title, category FROM events ORDER BY id")
    .all();
}
```

**Line by line:** the repository function accepts an application value rather than an Express request object. When a category exists, it runs a parameterized filtered query. Otherwise it returns the full collection. The function returns rows; it does not choose HTTP status codes or send responses.

This boundary keeps SQL/database responsibility separate from HTTP responsibility.

